 "findings": [
  {
   "evidence": "`Continuous.clm_bundle_inverse` in Hom.lean:199 only needs `[CompleteSpace F\u2081]` and `\u2200 x, (\u03d5 x).IsInvertible`. `CoordinateHom.ofContinuous` and `fiberMap_ofContinuous` in Descent.lean:202-225 work for arbitrary normed `F`, `G`. In FiniteRank.lean:206-224, `Fin A.rank \u2192 \ud835\udd5c` is used only to build `e x` via `LinearEquiv.toContinuousLinearEquiv`.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Topology/VectorBundle/FiniteRank.lean",
   "fix": "In `Descent.lean`, add a general `CoordinateHom.inverse (a : CoordinateHom Z W) (h : \u2200 x, (a.fiberMap x).IsInvertible) : CoordinateHom W Z` for `[CompleteSpace F]`, with `fiberMap_inverse`, `comp_inverse` and `inverse_comp`. Then derive `isIso_iff_bijective` from it, using finite dimensionality only to turn `Bijective` into `IsInvertible`.",
   "issue": "The reverse direction of `isIso_iff_bijective` builds the inverse morphism `g := CoordinateHom.ofContinuous (fun x => (f.fiberMap x).inverse) (f.continuous_fiberMap.clm_bundle_inverse \u2026 he)` and proves both inverse identities inline. Only the fibrewise `IsInvertible` input `he` uses finite dimensionality; the rest works for any `CoordinateHom Z W` with `[CompleteSpace F]`. The future variable-rank category on clopen strata would have to redo this proof.",
   "line": 206
  }
 ],
